{
  "name": "opencode-multi-llm",
  "version": "0.1.4",
  "description": "Run multi-LLM plan reviews, task generation and code reviews from inside OpenCode",
  "type": "module",
  "main": "./dist/index.mjs",
  "exports": {
    ".": "./dist/index.mjs",
    "./server": "./dist/index.mjs"
  },
  "files": ["dist", "skills", "README.md", "LICENSE"],
  "engines": {
    "opencode": ">=1.19.5 <2.0.0"
  },
  "keywords": ["opencode-plugin", "opencode", "multi-llm", "code-review"],
  "license": "MIT",
  "repository": "https://github.com/beastlabai/multi-llm-plugin",
  "scripts": {
    "prepack": "uv run --project ../../skills/multi-llm -- python build.py"
  },
  "devDependencies": {
    "@opencode-ai/plugin": "1.19.5"
  }
}

You are implementing a specific task from a larger plan.

## Plan Context
{plan_preamble}

## Plan Reference
Full plan: {plan_path}
Consult only if the above context leaves something genuinely ambiguous.

## Task
Title: {task_title}
Description: {task_description}

## Relevant Files to Review
{relevant_files}

Read these files to understand existing patterns before implementing.

## Output Files Expected
{output_files}

{acceptance_criteria_section}
{dependency_section}
## Changes Applied in Prior Batches
(Review these to avoid redoing work — do NOT re-apply these changes)

{{prior_changes_context}}

## Instructions
1. Read the relevant files above to understand existing patterns
2. Implement ONLY what is described in this task
3. Do not implement features from other tasks

## Constraints
- Do NOT run git commit, git push, or any destructive git operations
- Do NOT modify files outside the output_files list unless absolutely necessary
- Do NOT create unnecessary abstractions or over-engineer the solution
- Stay focused on the specific task at hand
- Only run tests directly related to this task's changed files — do NOT run broad test suites or regression checks
- If a test fails, be aware that other tasks may be running in parallel and modifying shared code — the failure may not be caused by your changes. Only fix failures clearly related to your own modifications.
